<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
<div><h1>Participatory governance for the age of AI.</h1><p class="lede">Where Singularity imagines AI making human contribution obsolete, we advance Plurality: keeping human agency and democracy at the wheel, and treating technology as a means of cooperating across difference. RadicalxChange Foundation is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit founded in 2018 by economist Glen Weyl in the wake of <a href="https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691196060/radical-markets"><i>Radical Markets</i></a>, and now the home of the movement that <a href="https://plurality.net/"><i>Plurality</i></a> extended.</p></div>
<div class="aside">RadicalxChange is both a Foundation and a global community. The Foundation runs projects with partners and publishes research; the <a href="/community/">community</a> tests the ideas in its own cities. <a href="/vision/">Read the longer vision</a>.</div>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><div><h2>From theory to practice</h2><p>Research alone doesn't shift power. Four strands of work reinforce each other, and the connective tissue between them is the Foundation.</p></div></div>
<div class="pillars">
<div><h3>Research</h3><p>Open papers, frameworks and proposals, from the founding academic work on plural voting and funding to the <a href="/projects/the-plural-stack/">Plural Stack</a>. <a href="/wiki/">The Library</a>.</p></div>
<div><h3>Civic-tech prototypes</h3><p>Turning ideas into working mechanisms: an open-source <a href="https://quadraticvote.radicalxchange.org/">plural voting tool</a>, partial common ownership of art, community currencies. <a href="/tools/">The tools</a>.</p></div>
<div><h3>Partnerships</h3><p>Building "civic muscle" with governments, institutions and community organisations, from the <a href="/projects/plural-voting-in-the-colorado-state-legislature/">Colorado legislature</a> to <a href="/density-done-well/">Sydney's density debate</a> to the <a href="/geneva-reflections/">UN Global Dialogue on AI</a> to <a href="/updates/announcements/2025-04-federated-data-bargaining-with-openmined/">500 Indonesian newsrooms bargaining collectively with AI companies</a>. <a href="/projects/">The projects</a>.</p></div>
<div><h3>Community</h3><p>A global network of chapters, Salons and a monthly call that tests these ideas across very different contexts. <a href="/community/">The community</a>.</p></div>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="section tint"><div class="wrap">
<div class="twocol">
<div><h3>Proof at national scale</h3><p>Taiwan's embrace of these methods under Audrey Tang is well known. The next iteration is emerging in Japan, where the <a href="https://plurality.net/read/">Plurality book</a> inspired <a href="https://www.techpolicy.press/japans-team-mirai-uses-tech-to-bolster-democracy-not-undermine-it/">Team Mirai</a>, an independent party using AI to help citizens understand and shape policy. In 2026 it won eleven parliamentary seats.</p></div>
<div><h3>Our role</h3><p>RadicalxChange is the connective tissue for this ecosystem: community work proves the methods on the ground, while ambitious, economy-scale proposals carry them to the grand challenges of our era. Both serve the same goal, helping humans steer the AI transition.</p></div>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
<div class="section-head"><div><h2>Team</h2></div></div>
<div class="people"><div><h3><a href="/team/jess-scully/" style="text-decoration:none">Jess Scully</a></h3><p class="role">Executive Director</p><p>Jess Scully is Executive Director of RadicalxChange and an advocate for civic imagination.</p></div><div><h3><a href="/team/jack-henderson/" style="text-decoration:none">Jack Henderson</a></h3><p class="role">Director of Operations</p><p>Jack Henderson is Director of Operations at RadicalxChange Foundation, where he focuses on accelerating institutional innovation to match the pace of technological innovation. His recent writing is focused on data coalitions, partial common ownership, and the future of work. Jack is from Pennsylvania, studied economics at Princeton, and is now based in Brooklyn.</p></div><div><h3><a href="/team/paula-berman/" style="text-decoration:none">Paula Berman</a></h3><p class="role">Director of Programs &amp; Partnerships</p><p>Paula Berman is a researcher and facilitator working with governments to expand citizen participation and pioneer new models of democratic governance. Her writing examines institutional design and the ways governance and technology can be structured to strengthen participation and resilience in democracy.</p></div></div>
